## Secondary Interfaces (Under-connected)

### Terminal CLI
- `src/io/terminal/` — Interactive REPL
- Currently **not wired** into the main bus in `main.rs`
- Would publish `chat_request` / `user_input` the same way the WebSocket does

### UNIX Domain Socket
- `src/io/unix_socket.rs`
- Local IPC for other processes on the same machine
- Not yet integrated into the main listener loop

### Cron / Autonomous Triggers
- Heartbeat and cron jobs publish `agent_run` messages
- These are consumed by the CPU or future `RuntimeLoop`

---

## Current Gaps in CLI/Web Layer

1. Terminal and UNIX socket are not subscribed to the bus at startup
2. No streaming responses yet (all LLM calls are non-streaming)
3. No authentication / multi-user support on the WebSocket
4. Web UI is the only fully functional input path today

